message: "If you use MLFCS in research, please cite the archived software release."
title: "MLFCS: arbitrary-order finite-difference force constants with ASE and JAX"
type: software
version: 3.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-03
authors:
  - given-names: "Yibo"
    family-names: "Gao"
    affiliation: "School of Physics, Central South University"
    email: "242211044@csu.edu.cn"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gtiders/mlfcs"
url: "https://github.com/gtiders/mlfcs"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - anharmonic force constants
  - finite differences
  - phonons
  - ASE
  - JAX
abstract: >-
  MLFCS reconstructs symmetry-reduced interatomic force constants from second to arbitrary
  order using recursive central finite differences and forces supplied through ASE calculators
  or external sow/reap workflows. It provides sparse storage, translational sum-rule projection,
  CPU/GPU tensor operations, and interoperable HDF5, phonopy, phono3py, and ShengBTE output.
